    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Effect of earlier staffing action",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section, 1989 direction means the direction given by the\nPublic Service Commissioner on 9 June 1989 under\nsubsection 33C(2) of the Public Service Act and relating to the\ninclusion of certain unattached officers in the ACT Branch.\n\n(2) The 1989 direction is to be taken to have had the effect of\nincluding in the ACT Branch the unattached officers to whom the\ndirection was expressed to apply and to have so included those\nofficers on 9 June 1989.\n\n(3) A person to whom this subsection applies is to be taken to have\nbeen, on 9 June 1989, included in the ACT Branch.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies to a person if:\n\n(a) the person was, on 9 June 1989, an unattached officer; and\n\n(b) the last office held by the person before that date was an\noffice the duties of which related, wholly or substantially, to\nmatters that, as at 9 June 1989, were dealt with by the ACT\nBranch.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this section, 1989 direction means the direction given by the\nPublic Service Commissioner on 9 June 1989 under\nsubsection 33C(2) of the Public Service Act and relating to the\ninclusion of certain unattached officers in the ACT Branch.\n\n(2) The 1989 direction is to be taken to have had the effect of\nincluding in the ACT Branch the unattached officers to whom the\ndirection was expressed to apply and to have so included those\nofficers on 9 June 1989.\n\n(3) A person to whom this subsection applies is to be taken to have\nbeen, on 9 June 1989, included in the ACT Branch.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies to a person if:\n\n(a) the person was, on 9 June 1989, an unattached officer; and\n\n(b) the last office held by the person before that date was an\noffice the duties of which related, wholly or substantially, to\nmatters that, as at 9 June 1989, were dealt with by the ACT\nBranch.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-4-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-4-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4787d0854aed5946dbc19af2a049e5598c21f6e19775374f197f12aa53bcfff4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Effect of earlier staffing action",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section, 1989 direction means the direction given by the\nPublic Service Commissioner on 9 June 1989 under\nsubsection 33C(2) of the Public Service Act and relating to the\ninclusion of certain unattached officers in the ACT Branch.\n\n(2) The 1989 direction is to be taken to have had the effect of\nincluding in the ACT Branch the unattached officers to whom the\ndirection was expressed to apply and to have so included those\nofficers on 9 June 1989.\n\n(3) A person to whom this subsection applies is to be taken to have\nbeen, on 9 June 1989, included in the ACT Branch.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies to a person if:\n\n(a) the person was, on 9 June 1989, an unattached officer; and\n\n(b) the last office held by the person before that date was an\noffice the duties of which related, wholly or substantially, to\nmatters that, as at 9 June 1989, were dealt with by the ACT\nBranch."
    },
