    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Transfer of personnel files",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies where before the commencement of the Public\nService Act 1999:\n\n(a) a person ceases to be an officer of the Australian Public\nService and becomes an ACT officer; or\n\n(b) a person ceases to be an ACT officer and becomes an officer\nof the Australian Public Service.\n\n(2) In a case referred to in paragraph (1)(a), the relevant Secretary or\nAgency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999)\nmay deliver to the appropriate authority of the Australian Capital\nTerritory all records kept by the Secretary or Agency Head in\nrelation to the person and reasonably necessary to be so delivered\n\n\nProvisions related to the establishment of the Australian Capital Territory Government\nService  Part 2\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Government Service (Consequential Provisions)\nAct 1994\nCompilation date: 18/10/2023\nRegistered: 14/11/2023\n\nin connection with the employment of the person as an ACT\nofficer.\n\n(3) In a case referred to in paragraph (1)(b), records kept, in relation to\nthe person, for the purposes of the Australian Capital Territory\nGovernment Service may be delivered to the relevant Secretary or\nAgency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999)\nif it is reasonably necessary for the records to be so delivered in\nconnection with the employment of the person as an officer of the\nAustralian Public Service.\n\n(4) Personal information contained in records delivered to an authority\nunder subsection (2) may be used as if the information had been\ncollected by the authority for the purposes of the Australian Capital\nTerritory Government Service.\n\n(5) Personal information contained in records delivered to a Secretary\nor Agency Head under subsection (3) may be used as if the\ninformation had been collected by the Secretary for the purposes of\nthe Australian Public Service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies where before the commencement of the Public\nService Act 1999:\n\n(a) a person ceases to be an officer of the Australian Public\nService and becomes an ACT officer; or\n\n(b) a person ceases to be an ACT officer and becomes an officer\nof the Australian Public Service.\n\n(2) In a case referred to in paragraph (1)(a), the relevant Secretary or\nAgency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999)\nmay deliver to the appropriate authority of the Australian Capital\nTerritory all records kept by the Secretary or Agency Head in\nrelation to the person and reasonably necessary to be so delivered\n\n\nProvisions related to the establishment of the Australian Capital Territory Government\nService  Part 2\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Government Service (Consequential Provisions)\nAct 1994\nCompilation date: 18/10/2023\nRegistered: 14/11/2023\n\nin connection with the employment of the person as an ACT\nofficer.\n\n(3) In a case referred to in paragraph (1)(b), records kept, in relation to\nthe person, for the purposes of the Australian Capital Territory\nGovernment Service may be delivered to the relevant Secretary or\nAgency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999)\nif it is reasonably necessary for the records to be so delivered in\nconnection with the employment of the person as an officer of the\nAustralian Public Service.\n\n(4) Personal information contained in records delivered to an authority\nunder subsection (2) may be used as if the information had been\ncollected by the authority for the purposes of the Australian Capital\nTerritory Government Service.\n\n(5) Personal information contained in records delivered to a Secretary\nor Agency Head under subsection (3) may be used as if the\ninformation had been collected by the Secretary for the purposes of\nthe Australian Public Service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-8-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-8-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-8-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-8-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-8-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4852374f688fcc7426cacaaf4a4ab34acfa389ac35308865daf695add6207f43"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Transfer of personnel files",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies where before the commencement of the Public\nService Act 1999:\n\n(a) a person ceases to be an officer of the Australian Public\nService and becomes an ACT officer; or\n\n(b) a person ceases to be an ACT officer and becomes an officer\nof the Australian Public Service.\n\n(2) In a case referred to in paragraph (1)(a), the relevant Secretary or\nAgency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999)\nmay deliver to the appropriate authority of the Australian Capital\nTerritory all records kept by the Secretary or Agency Head in\nrelation to the person and reasonably necessary to be so delivered\n\n\nProvisions related to the establishment of the Australian Capital Territory Government\nService  Part 2\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Government Service (Consequential Provisions)\nAct 1994\nCompilation date: 18/10/2023\nRegistered: 14/11/2023\n\nin connection with the employment of the person as an ACT\nofficer.\n\n(3) In a case referred to in paragraph (1)(b), records kept, in relation to\nthe person, for the purposes of the Australian Capital Territory\nGovernment Service may be delivered to the relevant Secretary or\nAgency Head (within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999)\nif it is reasonably necessary for the records to be so delivered in\nconnection with the employment of the person as an officer of the\nAustralian Public Service.\n\n(4) Personal information contained in records delivered to an authority\nunder subsection (2) may be used as if the information had been\ncollected by the authority for the purposes of the Australian Capital\nTerritory Government Service.\n\n(5) Personal information contained in records delivered to a Secretary\nor Agency Head under subsection (3) may be used as if the\ninformation had been collected by the Secretary for the purposes of\nthe Australian Public Service."
    },
