    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Leave entitlements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person who is engaged under section 22 of\nthe Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(3) If, immediately before a person to whom this section applies ceases\nto be an ACT officer, the person has an entitlement, as such an\nofficer, to leave of absence for recreation, the person retains that\nentitlement, on engagement as an APS employee, as if the\nentitlement had accrued under the Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(4) The Public Service Act 1999 has effect, in relation to the accrual,\non and after the engagement of a person as an APS employee, of\nthe person’s entitlement to leave of absence for recreation in\nrelation to a period since the person last gained an entitlement, as\nan ACT officer, to leave of absence for recreation as if service by\nthe person as an ACT officer during that period had been service as\nan APS employee.\n\n(5) If, immediately before the engagement of a person as an APS\nemployee, the person has an entitlement, as an ACT officer, to be\npaid a recreation leave loading, the person retains the entitlement\nas if the entitlement had accrued under the APS Award 1998, but\nthe entitlement is subject to the provisions of that award as if it had\narisen under that award.\n\n(6) The reference in subsection (5) to a recreation leave loading is a\nreference to a payment that corresponds, or substantially\ncorresponds, to a payment under the APS Award 1998.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a person who is engaged under section 22 of\nthe Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(3) If, immediately before a person to whom this section applies ceases\nto be an ACT officer, the person has an entitlement, as such an\nofficer, to leave of absence for recreation, the person retains that\nentitlement, on engagement as an APS employee, as if the\nentitlement had accrued under the Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(4) The Public Service Act 1999 has effect, in relation to the accrual,\non and after the engagement of a person as an APS employee, of\nthe person’s entitlement to leave of absence for recreation in\nrelation to a period since the person last gained an entitlement, as\nan ACT officer, to leave of absence for recreation as if service by\nthe person as an ACT officer during that period had been service as\nan APS employee.\n\n(5) If, immediately before the engagement of a person as an APS\nemployee, the person has an entitlement, as an ACT officer, to be\npaid a recreation leave loading, the person retains the entitlement\nas if the entitlement had accrued under the APS Award 1998, but\nthe entitlement is subject to the provisions of that award as if it had\narisen under that award.\n\n(6) The reference in subsection (5) to a recreation leave loading is a\nreference to a payment that corresponds, or substantially\ncorresponds, to a payment under the APS Award 1998.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "187e7a959e5e66bdfade5c143e16dd34ec6b1f108d29f64a06186724fd10f660"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Leave entitlements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person who is engaged under section 22 of\nthe Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(3) If, immediately before a person to whom this section applies ceases\nto be an ACT officer, the person has an entitlement, as such an\nofficer, to leave of absence for recreation, the person retains that\nentitlement, on engagement as an APS employee, as if the\nentitlement had accrued under the Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(4) The Public Service Act 1999 has effect, in relation to the accrual,\non and after the engagement of a person as an APS employee, of\nthe person’s entitlement to leave of absence for recreation in\nrelation to a period since the person last gained an entitlement, as\nan ACT officer, to leave of absence for recreation as if service by\nthe person as an ACT officer during that period had been service as\nan APS employee.\n\n(5) If, immediately before the engagement of a person as an APS\nemployee, the person has an entitlement, as an ACT officer, to be\npaid a recreation leave loading, the person retains the entitlement\nas if the entitlement had accrued under the APS Award 1998, but\nthe entitlement is subject to the provisions of that award as if it had\narisen under that award.\n\n(6) The reference in subsection (5) to a recreation leave loading is a\nreference to a payment that corresponds, or substantially\ncorresponds, to a payment under the APS Award 1998."
    },
