    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25(5) Leave entitlements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-25-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If, immediately before the engagement of a person as an APS\nemployee, the person has an entitlement, as an ACT officer, to be\npaid a recreation leave loading, the person retains the entitlement\nas if the entitlement had accrued under the APS Award 1998, but\nthe entitlement is subject to the provisions of that award as if it had\narisen under that award.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If, immediately before the engagement of a person as an APS\nemployee, the person has an entitlement, as an ACT officer, to be\npaid a recreation leave loading, the person retains the entitlement\nas if the entitlement had accrued under the APS Award 1998, but\nthe entitlement is subject to the provisions of that award as if it had\narisen under that award.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994-sec-25-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a51feaf990c27da4b835417a3f11fa0717afea844216d50ff8fcb51132efdc24",
      "skos:note": "Retains recreation leave loading entitlement as if it had accrued under the APS Award 1998."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-government-service-consequential-provisions-act-1994#sec-25-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25(5) Leave entitlements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If, immediately before the engagement of a person as an APS\nemployee, the person has an entitlement, as an ACT officer, to be\npaid a recreation leave loading, the person retains the entitlement\nas if the entitlement had accrued under the APS Award 1998, but\nthe entitlement is subject to the provisions of that award as if it had\narisen under that award."
    },
